    "headline": "What RUMIN holds on Aerisca Airways",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "role": "answer",
        "text": "Aerisca Airways is a fictional company in RUMIN's knowledge graph [E1]. RUMIN's record describes it as “Fictional Indian full-service airline” [E1].",
        "citations": ["E1"]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "role": "answer",
        "text": "The graph states 4 paths by which 4 economic variables reach it: 4 through costs [E2]. They start from Brent crude oil price, Jet fuel price (U.S. Gulf Coast), U.S. effective federal funds rate and USD/INR exchange rate [E2].",
        "citations": ["E2"]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "role": "answer",
        "text": "Its latest stored scenario execution, “Oil, rupee and rates on Aerisca” (version 1), simulated profit before tax falling by 6,700,000 INR over 12 months [E11]. That is a simulated result under the scenario's changes and entered figures, not a forecast.",
        "citations": ["E11"]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "role": "answer",
        "text": "Financial Intelligence lists 20 findings for it [E13]; the first reads “Official exchange rate (INR per US$, period average) — India rose 9.38 %” (evidence grade observed) [E14].",
        "citations": ["E13", "E14"]
      },
